variant smd of ../../hardware/graph.circuit
  set name "christmas-bell-smd"
  set version "0.1"
  set date "2026-10-26"
  description "Automatic Christmas bell, variant SMD (D-11): the circuit of the main board with 0805 LEDs, an SMD
      servo header and an SMD buffer capacitor; JLCPCB's Economic assembly places everything but the Nano's female
      headers."
  purpose private market EU
    notes "Automatic Christmas bell, SMD variant, for the owner's home, built and used by the owner – not sold or
        given away (D-16). Powered from a USB port or power bank through the Nano's USB; no battery holder, no mains,
        no radio."
  part J1 connector "HX PZ2.54-1x3P TP-YQ" lcsc C41417360 bom yes "Servo (GND, +5 V, signal), SMD header"
    notes "Standard servo plug: brown = GND (1), red = +5 V (2), orange = signal (3). SMD header, placed by JLCPCB
      (D-11)."
  part C1 capacitor "RVT1C102M1010 1000uF 16V SMD" lcsc C3359 bom yes "Buffer capacitor for the servo (SMD)"
    notes "Absorbs the servo's start-up peaks so the Nano does not reset. SMD can: the Economic assembly places it
      (D-11)."
  part LED5 led KT-0805G lcsc C2297 bom yes "0805 LED, green, countdown step 1"
    notes "D-11: KT-0805 series, pin 1 = anode, pin 2 = cathode (footprint mark at pad 2)"
  part LED4 led KT-0805G lcsc C2297 bom yes "0805 LED, green, countdown step 2"
    notes "D-11: KT-0805 series, pin 1 = anode, pin 2 = cathode (footprint mark at pad 2)"
  part LED3 led KT-0805Y lcsc C2296 bom yes "0805 LED, yellow, countdown step 3"
    notes "D-11: KT-0805 series, pin 1 = anode, pin 2 = cathode (footprint mark at pad 2)"
  part LED2 led KT-0805Y lcsc C2296 bom yes "0805 LED, yellow, countdown step 4"
    notes "D-11: KT-0805 series, pin 1 = anode, pin 2 = cathode (footprint mark at pad 2)"
  part LED1 led KT-0805R lcsc C2295 bom yes "0805 LED, red, countdown step 5"
    notes "D-11: KT-0805 series, pin 1 = anode, pin 2 = cathode (footprint mark at pad 2)"
  accept HINT.bulk "C1 1000 µF / 16 V electrolytic on +5V, next to J1 (it buffers the Nano's 5V pin)"
  accept HINT.debounce "debounced in firmware: src/firmware/buttons.ino, 50 ms (DEBOUNCE_DELAY)"
  accept HINT.esd "J1 is the servo's own cable inside the bell's frame, plugged once; no TVS – like the main board"
